        "checked_on": "2026-11-16",
        "scope": "Selected HTTP/SIP access, native code-flow constraints, service authorization and identity binding, token refresh, partner-token exchange and migration authorization, KMS roles/provisioning, on-network private-key distribution, group-key delivery and membership-change handling. External security profiles, complete OIDC/JWT validation, full KRR/MIKEY/SRTP and call state machines remain unchecked. Also selected UE key persistence/deletion triggers and group SRTP derivation inputs versus on-network/off-network SRTCP protection boundaries; complete algorithms and Annex H remain unchecked. MC gateway two-layer authentication and forwarding boundaries checked in 5.12.1; referenced TS33.501 not checked. Selected initial CSK upload, per-server CSK replacement and MuSiK rejection/unicast boundary checked. Selected public-safety XML application-layer activation, content scope, integrity-body coverage and MC-server visibility checked; W3C implementation/KDF remains unchecked. Selected MCData signalling/data key roles, private SDS/FD reuse, protection versus authentication prerequisites and visible protected-payload metadata checked; full Stage3 formats and algorithms remain unchecked. Protected multi-talker MCPTT mixing/forwarding and preconfigured group/user regroup key prerequisites checked. Bounded KRR purpose, policy narrowing, Home-domain trust and hold/deny controls checked; ambiguous selection and signed-policy wording explicitly unresolved, no selection algorithm claimed. Token response ID/refresh optionality compared against TS24.482 V19.0.0 without resolving cross-document obligations."
      },
